AUDIO: 'Hey everybody, it\'s Linus Tech Tips and I\'ve got an update for you all on my Intel powered AI rig here. If you recall in my last video, I talked about this 32 GB Intel B760 GPU I picked up the other day. This has 32 GB of video RAM on'

[00:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'board and is I think still the least expensive 32 GB card on the market. A lot of people are wondering about video and image generation and I was totally blown away by what you can do with local'

[00:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'AI right now. This is Comfy UI, which is kind of a wrapper for different models that you can install. And on here right now, I\'ve got Minimax H3 running and it just generated this awesome looking'

[00:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'scene here. This was all generated on this GPU and the Comfy UI here has an Intel optimized version, which makes it run fairly well. And right now, most of the model can fit on the GPU, although'

[00:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it does offload some to the system memory. And what I\'m going to do here real quick is change this prompt. What we\'re going to do is give it a new version, which is essentially the same action here, but we\'re going to have it'

[01:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'based in the Super Mario Brothers universe. This one was based off of a template that was built into Comfy UI. Now right now, you\'ll see it\'s only running for about 5 seconds. That\'s kind of the sweet spot with this, but I have'

[01:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'been able to generate slightly longer clips. They just take longer to generate. So, what I thought I would do here first to kick things off is I\'ll go ahead and hit the run button here along with a timer on my phone. And what we\'ll do is we\'ll see how long it takes for'

[01:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this setup here to revise the this video and work with the new prompt. And as my rig here starts to chew on this, I do want to let you know in the interest of full disclosure that I paid for the GPU with my own funds, but the OcuLink dock'

[01:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that it is plugged into along with the Minisforum PC here at the bottom came in free of charge from their respective manufacturers for some reviews that I did a little while back. However, no other compensation was received. All of'

