VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the opinions you\'re about to hear are my own, and no one has reviewed or approved what you\'re about to see before it was uploaded. So, let\'s take a look at what we\'ve got cooking in this GPU now and see what it generated and how long it'

[02:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'took. All right, it is done. I have not played this yet. I want to watch it for the first time along with you. And as you can see on my phone here, it took 2 minutes and 36 seconds essentially to put this together, which isn\'t bad. But,'

[02:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'why don\'t we play the video here and see how it came out. So, I think it did a pretty good job here. I\'ve actually been really impressed with the quality of this model and how relatively quickly it can spit'

[02:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'stuff out. Now, granted, this was a very short clip and not a very high resolution, so we had it running for 5 seconds as you can see here. And if we go down to the resolution, you can see it\'s set to 0.4 megapixels, which'

[02:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'amounts to basically a 480p output. But, we can go up to what looks like about 1080p on this. So, you can get higher quality, but you start to get into issues with performance when you really'

[03:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'crank things up. But, for quick outputs here, I think the image generation is pretty impressive for a model that runs totally locally on this device. Let me show you a couple of other ones that I'

